<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" /><title>HCI Long Quiz 1 - Complete 1-70</title><style> :root{--bg:#f7f9fc;--card:#fff;--text:#1f2937;--muted:#6b7280;--accent:#2563eb;--accent2:#0f766e;--border:#e5e7eb;--answer-bg:#f0fdf4;--answer-border:#86efac;--shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(15,23,42,.08);--radius:18px}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background:linear-gradient(180deg,#eef4ff 0%,#f7f9fc 25%,#fff 100%);color:var(--text);line-height:1.55}.container{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:24px 16px 60px}.hero{background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1d4ed8,#0f766e);color:#fff;border-radius:24px;padding:28px 24px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:18px}.hero h1{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:2rem;line-height:1.1}.hero p{margin:6px 0 0;max-width:860px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.92)}.controls{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0 22px}button{border:0;border-radius:999px;padding:12px 16px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;transition:transform .15s ease,box-shadow .15s ease}button:hover{transform:translateY(-1px)}.btn-primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(37,99,235,.22)}.btn-secondary{background:#e5e7eb;color:#111827}.btn-success{background:var(--accent2);color:#fff;box-shadow:0 8px 20px rgba(15,118,110,.18)}.section{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius);box-shadow:var(--shadow);margin-bottom:20px;overflow:hidden}.section-header{padding:18px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);background:#fbfdff}.section-header h2{margin:0;font-size:1.35rem}.section-header p{margin:6px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}.item{padding:18px 20px;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.q{font-weight:700;margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1rem}.answer{display:none;margin-top:10px;padding:12px 14px;border-radius:14px;background:var(--answer-bg);border:1px solid var(--answer-border)}.answer strong{color:#166534}.toggle-answer{margin-top:8px;background:#dbeafe;color:#1d4ed8;padding:9px 14px;font-size:.92rem}.choice-list{margin:8px 0 0 18px;padding:0}.choice-list li{margin:4px 0}.footer-note{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;margin-top:8px}.tag{display:inline-block;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:999px;background:#eff6ff;color:#1d4ed8;font-size:.82rem;font-weight:700;margin-top:8px}@media (max-width:800px){.hero h1{font-size:1.6rem}}</style></head><body><div class="container"><div class="hero"><h1>Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) Long Quiz 1</h1><p>Complete version with all questions numbered 1–70. Click any answer button to reveal the answer.</p></div><div class="controls"><button class="btn-primary" onclick="showAllAnswers()">Show All Answers</button><button class="btn-secondary" onclick="hideAllAnswers()">Hide All Answers</button><button class="btn-success" onclick="window.print()">Print / Save as PDF</button></div><div class="section"><div class="section-header"><h2>Part I: Multiple Choice</h2><p>Choose the best answer for each item.</p></div><div class="item"><div class="q">1. Providing a "Payment Successful" message on an e-commerce app satisfies which rule?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Design Dialogs to Yield Closure</li><li>b) Offer Informative Feedback</li><li>c) Strive for Consistency</li><li>d) Permit Easy Reversal of Actions</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Offer Informative Feedback</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">2. A developer for a popular Philippine e-wallet (like GCash) uses the same blue color and font style across all its mini-apps. Which rule is being applied?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Support Internal Locus of Control</li><li>b) Strive for Consistency</li><li>c) Offer Simple Error Handling</li><li>d) Seek Universal Usability</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Strive for Consistency</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">3. Which device is considered essential for text input and command execution?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Mouse</li><li>b) Trackpad</li><li>c) Keyboard</li><li>d) Scanner</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Keyboard</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">4. Which interaction paradigm shift was most responsible for revolutionizing engagement with smartphones?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Voice Recognition</li><li>b) Graphical User Interface</li><li>c) Touch Interface</li><li>d) Gesture Control</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Touch Interface</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">5. Which interaction paradigm involves voice recognition technology?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Touch Interaction</li><li>b) Gesture Control</li><li>c) Voice Interaction</li><li>d) Traditional Input</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Voice Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">6. A food delivery app in Makati asks, "Would you like to receive notifications for your rider's location?" and gives a "Maybe Later" option. This supports:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Internal Locus of Control</li><li>b) Universal Usability</li><li>c) Informative Feedback</li><li>d) Consistency</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> a) Internal Locus of Control</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">7. What are the three major components of HCI?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Hardware, Software, Network</li><li>b) The User, The Computer, The Interaction</li><li>c) Input, Output, Storage</li><li>d) People, Process, Technology</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) The User, The Computer, The Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">8. Which rule ensures a system serves everyone, including those with disabilities?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Strive for Consistency</li><li>b) Seek Universal Usability</li><li>c) Offer Informative Feedback</li><li>d) Support Internal Locus of Control</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Seek Universal Usability</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">9. While using a registration portal for a Philippine university, a student gets an error: "Invalid Birthday Format (use MM/DD/YYYY)." This message is:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) A prompt for Closure</li><li>b) Simple Error Handling</li><li>c) Internal Locus of Control</li><li>d) Consistency</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Simple Error Handling</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">10. Who developed the "8 Golden Rules" of interface design?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Bill Gates</li><li>b) Ben Shneiderman</li><li>c) Steve Jobs</li><li>d) Rolie Elemia</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Ben Shneiderman</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">11. What is the primary focus of HCI?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Building faster processors</li><li>b) Designing user-friendly and efficient technologies</li><li>c) Developing complex algorithms</li><li>d) Increasing storage capacity</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Designing user-friendly and efficient technologies</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">12. Situational: A student in Manila is using a government website to apply for a valid ID. After submitting, a progress bar shows "Step 3 of 4." This provides:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Internal Locus of Control</li><li>b) Simple Error Handling</li><li>c) A "Sense of Relief" through Closure</li><li>d) Universal Usability</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) A "Sense of Relief" through Closure</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">13. Situational: During a "Flash Sale" on Shopee, the app prevents a user from clicking "Buy Now" if the item is out of stock. This is an example of:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Offering Simple Error Handling</li><li>b) Offering Informative Feedback</li><li>c) Striving for Consistency</li><li>d) Designing Dialogs for Closure</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> a) Offering Simple Error Handling (Error prevention)</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">14. Which device facilitates navigation through a touch-sensitive surface?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Keyboard</li><li>b) Mouse</li><li>c) Trackpad</li><li>d) Monitor</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Trackpad</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">15. Why is HCI considered a multidisciplinary field?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) It only involves coding.</li><li>b) It involves people, machines, and the interaction between them.</li><li>c) It is only used in classrooms.</li><li>d) It is strictly a hardware discipline.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) It involves people, machines, and the interaction between them.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">16. What does "IPO" stand for in the context of interaction?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Input, Process, Output</li><li>b) Internal, Program, Output</li><li>c) Input, Peripheral, Operation</li><li>d) Internal, Process, Operation</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> a) Input, Process, Output</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">17. A grandfather in the province uses "Hey Siri" to call his grandson because he finds small buttons difficult to press. This highlights:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Accuracy Challenges</li><li>b) Convenience and Accessibility</li><li>c) Privacy Concerns</li><li>d) Gesture Control</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Convenience and Accessibility</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">18. A smartphone is an example of which HCI component?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) The User</li><li>b) The Interaction</li><li>c) The Computer</li><li>d) Feedback</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) The Computer</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">19. Which interaction type allows users to engage without traditional controllers?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Keyboard entry</li><li>b) Gesture and Motion Sensing</li><li>c) Mouse clicking</li><li>d) Voice recognition</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Gesture and Motion Sensing</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">20. A Filipino gamer uses a VR headset that tracks hand movements to cast spells. This is an example of:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Voice Interaction</li><li>b) Gesture and Motion Sensing</li><li>c) Traditional Input</li><li>d) Graphical User Interface</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Gesture and Motion Sensing</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">21. Which of the following describes "Internal Locus of Control"?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) The computer tells the user what to do at all times.</li><li>b) The user feels they are in charge and initiating actions.</li><li>c) The system reboots automatically without warning.</li><li>d) The interface is designed for experts only.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) The user feels they are in charge and initiating actions.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">22. How does HCI boost productivity and efficiency?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) By making the computer more expensive.</li><li>b) By streamlining tasks and reducing user effort.</li><li>c) By adding more buttons to the interface.</li><li>d) By requiring specialized training for every app.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) By streamlining tasks and reducing user effort.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">23. You are building a localized weather app. You use a "sun" icon for Manila and the same "sun" icon for Cebu. This helps users build a:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Mental Model</li><li>b) New Mental Load</li><li>c) Feedback Loop</li><li>d) Gesture Control</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> a) Mental Model</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">24. What is a significant challenge of Voice Interaction?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) It is too fast.</li><li>b) Accuracy and privacy concerns.</li><li>c) It requires a mouse.</li><li>d) It only works on laptops.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Accuracy and privacy concerns.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">25. What does "Informative Feedback" indicate to the user?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) The price of the software.</li><li>b) The current system status.</li><li>c) The developer's name.</li><li>d) The history of HCI.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) The current system status.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">26. Multi-touch interaction is best described as:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Using one finger for all tasks.</li><li>b) Multiple fingers enabling advanced interactions.</li><li>c) Using a keyboard and mouse simultaneously.</li><li>d) A hands-free interaction method.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Multiple fingers enabling advanced interactions.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">27. "Design Dialogs to Yield Closure" aims to provide what psychological effect for the user?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Confusion</li><li>b) "Sense of Relief"</li><li>c) High Cognitive Load</li><li>d) Anxiety</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) "Sense of Relief"</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">28. Which rule is specifically mentioned as being supported by the companies Lenovo and Dovetail?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Offer Simple Error Handling</li><li>b) Increase Accessibility & Inclusivity</li><li>c) Strive for Consistency</li><li>d) Drive Innovation</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Increase Accessibility & Inclusivity</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">29. In the context of HCI, what is the role of an "Embedded System" like a microwave?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) It is not part of HCI study.</li><li>b) It represents computing technology people interact with daily.</li><li>c) It is a traditional desktop computer.</li><li>d) It only provides output, never input.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) It represents computing technology people interact with daily.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">30. Which rule is most closely linked to "mental models"?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Offer Informative Feedback</li><li>b) Strive for Consistency</li><li>c) Support Internal Locus of Control</li><li>d) Design Dialogs to Yield Closure</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Strive for Consistency</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">31. The introduction of Windows 1.0 was significant because:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) It was the first voice-activated system.</li><li>b) It introduced the first GUI operating system with windows.</li><li>c) It removed the need for a mouse.</li><li>d) It was an embedded system.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) It introduced the first GUI operating system with windows.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">32. How does HCI "Drive Innovation"?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) By keeping designs exactly the same for 20 years.</li><li>b) By encouraging creative thinking for new interaction methods.</li><li>c) By focusing only on traditional input devices.</li><li>d) By increasing the cost of hardware.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) By encouraging creative thinking for new interaction methods.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">33. What does "HCI" stand for?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Human-Center Integration</li><li>b) High-Computer Interaction</li><li>c) Human-Computer Interaction</li><li>d) Human-Computer Interface</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Human-Computer Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">34. What is the primary focus of HCI in the module?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Building faster processors</li><li>b) Designing user-friendly and efficient technologies</li><li>c) Developing complex algorithms</li><li>d) Increasing storage capacity</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Designing user-friendly and efficient technologies</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">35. Situational: A student in Manila is using a government website to apply for a valid ID. After submitting, a progress bar shows "Step 3 of 4." This provides:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Internal Locus of Control</li><li>b) Simple Error Handling</li><li>c) A "Sense of Relief" through Closure</li><li>d) Universal Usability</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) A "Sense of Relief" through Closure</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">36. Situational: During a "Flash Sale" on Shopee, the app prevents a user from clicking "Buy Now" if the item is out of stock. This is an example of:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Offering Simple Error Handling</li><li>b) Offering Informative Feedback</li><li>c) Striving for Consistency</li><li>d) Designing Dialogs for Closure</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> a) Offering Simple Error Handling (Error prevention)</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">37. Which of the following describes "Internal Locus of Control"?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) The computer tells the user what to do at all times.</li><li>b) The user feels they are in charge and initiating actions.</li><li>c) The system reboots automatically without warning.</li><li>d) The interface is designed for experts only.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) The user feels they are in charge and initiating actions.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">38. What does "Informative Feedback" indicate to the user?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) The price of the software.</li><li>b) The current system status.</li><li>c) The developer's name.</li><li>d) The history of HCI.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) The current system status.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">39. Multi-touch interaction is best described as:</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Using one finger for all tasks.</li><li>b) Multiple fingers enabling advanced interactions.</li><li>c) Using a keyboard and mouse simultaneously.</li><li>d) A hands-free interaction method.</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> b) Multiple fingers enabling advanced interactions.</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">40. What does "HCI" stand for?</div><ul class="choice-list"><li>a) Human-Center Integration</li><li>b) High-Computer Interaction</li><li>c) Human-Computer Interaction</li><li>d) Human-Computer Interface</li></ul><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> c) Human-Computer Interaction</div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-header"><h2>Part II: Identification</h2><p>Write the correct term or name.</p></div><div class="item"><div class="q">41. The multidisciplinary field focused on designing and implementing user-friendly computer technologies.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Human-Computer Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">42. A person or human being interacting with a system.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> User</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">43. This interaction paradigm revolutionized user engagement via smartphones.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Touch Interface</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">44. The specific golden rule that suggests using "Ctrl + Z" for undoing actions.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Permit Easy Reversal of Actions</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">45. Technology that allows hands-free device control through speech.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Voice Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">46. A programmable electronic device designed to process and store data.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Computer</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">47. This component of HCI includes smartphones and laptops.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Computer</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">48. The golden rule that emphasizes designing for both novices and experts.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Seek Universal Usability</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">49. These simplified user interactions and navigation significantly in early GUIs.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Icons</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">50. The psychological "sense" a user feels when a dialog signals the end of a task.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Closure / Sense of Relief</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">51. An example of a traditional input device used for clicking and navigation.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Mouse</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">52. This golden rule focuses on preventing errors and providing clear messages.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Offer Simple Error Handling</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">53. The name of the person who created the "8 Golden Rules."</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Ben Shneiderman</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">54. A touch-sensitive surface for intuitive navigation, often found on laptops.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Trackpad</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">55. This interaction type uses motion sensors to create new ways to interact.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Gesture and Motion Sensing</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">56. The specific goal of HCI that ensures technology serves everyone, including those with disabilities.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Accessibility / Universal Usability</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">57. The first GUI operating system that introduced windows.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Windows 1.0</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">58. This rule makes users feel they are initiating actions rather than just responding.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Internal Locus of Control</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">59. Advanced interaction experiences enabled by using multiple fingers.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Multi-touch Interaction</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">60. The immediate, clear, and relevant response given to every user action.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Informative Feedback</div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-header"><h2>Part III: True or False</h2><p>Write TRUE if the statement is correct and FALSE if it is wrong.</p></div><div class="item"><div class="q">61. A Filipino student using a tool finds that the "Save" icon is a "Trash Can" icon. This interface follows the rule of "Strive for Consistency."</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (It is inconsistent and confusing).</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">62. If the BPI app sends a push notification saying "Your transaction was successful," it is following the rule "Offer Informative Feedback."</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> TRUE</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">63. A smart traffic light in Quezon City that adjusts timing based on vehicle sensors is an example of an embedded system within the scope of HCI.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> TRUE</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">64. An ATM in a Manila mall that only allows English as a language option, even if users prefer Tagalog, is successfully "Seeking Universal Usability."</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (It excludes users who are not proficient in English).</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">65. A user in Pasig accidentally deletes an email and is able to hit "Undo" immediately. This reduces user anxiety.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> TRUE</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">66. HCI is strictly limited to the study of desktop computers and laptops.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (It includes smartphones, VR, embedded systems, etc.).</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">67. One of the goals of HCI is to increase cognitive load for the user.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (The goal is to reduce cognitive load).</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">68. "IPO" stands for Internal Productivity Optimization.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (It stands for Input, Process, Output).</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">69. Well-designed interfaces help users complete work faster and reduce effort.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> TRUE</div></div><div class="item"><div class="q">70. Gesture control technology is considered a traditional input device.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> FALSE (It is a post-WIMP/modern interaction paradigm).</div></div></div><div class="section"><div class="section-header"><h2>Bonus</h2><p>Additional item included in the reconstruction.</p></div><div class="item"><div class="q">Full name of your HCI Course Teacher.</div><button class="toggle-answer" onclick="toggleAnswer(this)">Show Answer</button><div class="answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Rolie L. Elemia</div></div></div><div class="footer-note">Tip: Save this file as <strong>.html</strong> and open it in any browser.</div><div class="tag">Self-contained study guide</div></div><script>function toggleAnswer(button){const answer=button.nextElementSibling;const open=answer.style.display==='block';answer.style.display=open?'none':'block';button.textContent=open?'Show Answer':'Hide Answer';}function showAllAnswers(){document.querySelectorAll('.answer').forEach(a=>a.style.display='block');document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-answer').forEach(b=>b.textContent='Hide Answer');}function hideAllAnswers(){document.querySelectorAll('.answer').forEach(a=>a.style.display='none');document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-answer').forEach(b=>b.textContent='Show Answer');}</script></body></html>
